# Same reason, second purge 2026-08-02. These two survived the first sweep because
# it targeted docs/research/ only, and they sat public for four days. DOMAIN-RULES.md
# named a sponsor's HEOR function and an internal consultancy handbook as its sources;
# MARKETSCAN-BRD.md keyed its highest confidence tag to the licensed Merative data
# dictionary. Domain facts belong in the code beside what they govern, sourced from
# public documentation only. Do not recreate either path.
docs/DOMAIN-RULES.md
docs/MARKETSCAN-BRD.md

# .github/workflows/ is tracked. Editing it needs a token carrying the
# "workflow" scope; without it every push of this tree is rejected whole, not
# just the workflow file. If that happens: gh auth refresh -h github.com -s workflow

